b196e14579e1106d166448fdcabb2088562b3f44
feat(a11y): mark the active sidebar link with aria-current="page"

Closes part of #957 (step 2, second half).

`<x-menu activate-by-route>` signalled the current page with the
`mary-active-menu` class and nothing else — a colour and a background. A
screen reader therefore heard an undifferentiated list of links with no idea
where the user actually was.

Same reasoning as the table override: the active state is decided inside
Mary's MenuItem::render(), so no attribute at the call site can express it.
AccessibleMenuItem mirrors that render and adds `aria-current="page"` under
the exact same condition as the class, so the visual and the announced state
cannot drift.

`mary-active-menu` is kept deliberately: Mary's MenuSub opens a submenu with
`Str::contains($slot, 'mary-active-menu')` over the already-rendered child
markup. The test asserts the enclosing <details> is still open, because losing
the class would collapse every submenu while the link test stayed green.
